        "original_id": "581d0fb2-8861-5b44-803b-ca83e15a7f44",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Patrick Carpentier, Ken Schrader\n- Organizations: NASCAR Sprint Cup Series, Go FAS Racing, NASCAR Craftsman Truck Series\n- Products: Ford Fusion, Lincoln MKZ, Mercury Milan\n- Places: Ford Hermosillo Stamping & Assembly plant, Saugus Speedway\n- Concepts: CD3 platform, Rookie of the Year\n- Events: 1997 CART season, 1995 NASCAR Craftsman Truck Series event\n\nFacts:\n- In 1995, Saugus Speedway hosted one NASCAR Craftsman Truck Series event, and Ken Schrader won that event.\n- In the 1997 CART season, Patrick Carpentier was Rookie of the Year.\n- The Ford Fusion was introduced for the 2006 model year.\n- The Ford Fusion is manufactured at Ford's Hermosillo Stamping & Assembly plant alongside the Lincoln MKZ, and it was formerly manufactured alongside the discontinued Mercury Milan.\n- The Ford Fusion, Lincoln MKZ, and Mercury Milan share the CD3 platform.\n- Patrick Carpentier was born on August 13, 1971, and he is a Canadian professional auto racing driver.\n- Patrick Carpentier currently competes part-time in the NASCAR Sprint Cup Series, driving the No. 32 Ford Fusion for Go FAS Racing.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
